\title{VC Dimension}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Our next question is the following: rather than concern ourselves with \em{computational efficiency} (e.g. “is this efficiently PAC?”), can we say anything about its \em{information theoretic efficiency}?}

\p{In other words, given a class #{\mathcal{C}}, can we limit the number of samples needed to reach PAC?}

\p{If #{|\mathcal{H}| < \infty} then we just did this with Generalised Occam’s Razor: if #{|\mathcal{H}| < \infty}, then #{\mathcal{C}} is PAC using #{\mathcal{H}}, provided a consistent learner and at least}

##{m \geq O\Big( \frac{1}{\varepsilon}\log\frac{|\mathcal{H}|}{\delta} \Big)}

\p{samples. Recall our first problem of the rectangle game had so many hypotheses.}

